From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:00:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: Do not take requests off a dead ring

When a frontend disconnects from a ring that still has requests in
flight, tapdisk keeps the ring as dead until they complete. The frontend
has seen the ring closed by then: any request it had pushed but tapdisk
had not yet taken may have had its grants revoked or reissued for other
pages.

Requests already taken from the dead ring still complete as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/td-blkif.c |  7 ++++++-
 drivers/td-ctx.c   | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/td-blkif.c b/drivers/td-blkif.c
index 0f3b16eb..e8767177 100644
--- a/drivers/td-blkif.c
+++ b/drivers/td-blkif.c
@@ -292,6 +292,7 @@ tapdisk_xenblkif_disconnect(const domid_t domid, const int devid)
     if (!blkif)
         return -ENODEV;
 
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&blkif->mutex);
     if (tapdisk_xenblkif_reqs_pending(blkif)) {
         RING_DEBUG(blkif, "disconnect from ring with %d pending requests\n",
                 blkif->ring_size - blkif->n_reqs_free);
@@ -320,9 +321,13 @@ tapdisk_xenblkif_disconnect(const domid_t domid, const int devid)
          * in tapdisk? IIUC if we don't unmap it we'll get errors during grant
          * copy.
          */
+
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&blkif->mutex);
         return 0;
-	} else
+    } else {
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&blkif->mutex);
         return tapdisk_xenblkif_destroy(blkif);
+    }
 }
 
 
diff --git a/drivers/td-ctx.c b/drivers/td-ctx.c
index a67fec01..a0fc40c5 100644
--- a/drivers/td-ctx.c
+++ b/drivers/td-ctx.c
@@ -295,7 +295,17 @@ tapdisk_xenio_ctx_process_ring(struct td_xenblkif *blkif,
     blkif_request_t **reqs;
     int limit;
 
+    /*
+     * Do not take requests off a dead ring: its frontend has closed it, and
+     * the grants of whatever it left on the shared ring may have been
+     * revoked or reissued.
+     */
     pthread_mutex_lock(&blkif->mutex);
+    if (unlikely(blkif->dead)) {
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&blkif->mutex);
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     start = blkif->n_reqs_free;
 
     if (unlikely(blkif->barrier.msg)) {
